 layout='Exactly FOUR equal independent square material variants arranged in a precise 2x2 canvas, no gutters, dividing lines, margins or borders. Each quadrant is a complete whole variant. The exact canvas halves determine the four crops. Match material palette and scale across quadrants.' if mode=='variants' else 'Exactly ONE continuous full-square repeatable material, NOT a sheet or four variants. Uniform ground fills the entire square edge to edge. The material will be sampled into a tiny central core and narrow cardinal connector strips.'
 prompt=f'Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: native32 tactical game terrain source master. Primary request: c03-terrain-{slug}, {label}. Image 1 is SUBJECT EVIDENCE ONLY: TOP ROW column {col} of the original atlas. Ignore all other atlas cells and its detailed old rendering style. Images 2 and 3 show approved BROAD MATTE surface simplification only; do not copy sci-fi subjects, colors, circuitry, metal or geometric paving. Subject: {subject} Composition: strictly orthographic overhead, flat playable ground. {layout} Output opaque SQUARE 1254 by 1254 canvas. Style: Legends of Kingdom Rush-inspired exaggerated chunky hand-painted cartoon terrain, bold readable shapes, restrained dark contours, few large matte color planes. Simplify even more than the two style references. Every surface uses only one base color plus one broad shadow plane, no extra shading patches. Absolutely NO granular mottling, painterly microtexture, brush grain, speckle, tiny marks, secondary facets, scratches, realistic noise, little cracks, glints, glossy shading, tiny decorations, text, labels, perspective horizon or watermark. Native32 readability is the priority. Do not subdivide the clean planes.'
 req={'slug':slug,'topicId':'c03-terrain-'+slug,'label':label,'tileMode':mode,'prompt':prompt,'referenced_image_paths':refs,'transparent_background':False}; requests.append(req)
 (d/'request.json').write_text(json.dumps(req,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)); (d/'prompt.txt').write_text(prompt+'\n')
